; M4 gate: a (break) whose landing sits inside its LOOP_END's own event, with
; the stream factored into CALLs between the two (opcodes.md §5.2). The paths
; into the join disagree (the vel macro and :gate-), so the encoder pins the
; state just past the LOOP_END in the same event, and the break lands ahead of
; the pins. The body past the break repeats after the loop, so the dedup
; factors it and the skip has to shrink with it — left as it was, the break
; landed mid-instruction and the track stopped.
(def env1 (macro :vel* [ (linear 15..11 :len 1t) (wait key-off) (linear 11..0 :len 65t) ]))
(sqr1 :tempo 150 env1 :oct 4 :vel 12 :len 16 :gate- 10t
  (x 3 c d e f (break) g a b > c < g a b > c <) g a b > c < g a b > c < c4)
